  "description": "The Eiffel Issue Verified event\u202f#123e4567\u2011e89b\u201112d3\u2011a456\u2011426614174000 (type\u202fEiffelIssueVerifiedEvent, version\u202f1.1.0) was recorded at Unix time\u202f1718425600 and is tagged \u201cverification\u201d and \u201cissue\u201d. It originated from the CI system at\u202fci.example.com, domain\u202fcom.example.project, under the name\u202fEiffelVerifier. The serializer that produced the payload is\u202fcom.example:eiffel-serializer:2.0.1 and the source URI is\u202fhttps://ci.example.com/builds/1234. For security, the SDM author is\u202fjohn.doe@example.com and the encrypted digest attached to the event is\u202fa1b2c3d4e5f67890abcdeffedcba9876.\n\nDuring this run two issues were verified. The first is a BUG tracked in Jira with ID\u202fPROJ\u2011123 (https://jira.example.com/browse/PROJ-123) and its verification result is\u202fSUCCESS. The second is a FEATURE recorded in Github with ID\u202f42 (https://github.com/org/repo/issues/42) and its verification result is\u202fFAILURE. The custom data field records the environment as \u201cstaging\u201d. This event is linked to the preceding cause event\u202f987f6543\u2011e21c\u201134b5\u2011b678\u2011123456789abc via a CAUSE link.",
